From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 22:52:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: ACPI: processor_idle: Preserve maximum LPI
 wake latency

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

Each _LPI wake latency is encoded as a DWORD, while OSPM adds the values
when composing states across hierarchy levels. A raw U32_MAX latency is
therefore dropped today because adding any nonzero child latency overflows
the composite DWORD.

Treat U32_MAX as saturated while composing the hierarchy. This preserves a
maximum-valued state for the existing selection policy: finite runtime-idle
constraints continue to exclude it, while an unconstrained suspend-to-idle
transition can reach it. Continue rejecting addition overflow when both
inputs are ordinary finite values.

Minimum residency remains the value supplied by the selected parent level;
ACPI does not define it as an additive hierarchy value.

Fixes: d7f4eee42f48 ("NVIDIA: SAUCE: ACPI: processor_idle: Correct hierarchical LPI composition")
Link: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301
Signed-off-by: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Co-developed-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Assisted-by: OpenAI-Codex:gpt-5.6
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
Ledger-Change: C-02139
Ledger-Origin: nvidia-bos@d711ace70221e6aa08a60e6e42863a5194ccbaae
---
 include/acpi/processor.h | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/acpi/processor.h b/include/acpi/processor.h
index f134f0992c75..a5c3a83267ba 100644
--- a/include/acpi/processor.h
+++ b/include/acpi/processor.h
@@ -132,8 +132,16 @@ acpi_processor_combine_lpi_states(const struct acpi_lpi_state *local,
 	 * state's value therefore becomes the composite value at this level.
 	 */
 	result->min_residency = parent->min_residency;
-	if (check_add_overflow(local->wake_latency, parent->wake_latency,
-			       &result->wake_latency))
+	/*
+	 * Preserve the maximum representable latency when a hierarchy level
+	 * adds to it. Other finite overflows still make the composite invalid.
+	 */
+	if (local->wake_latency == U32_MAX ||
+	    parent->wake_latency == U32_MAX)
+		result->wake_latency = U32_MAX;
+	else if (check_add_overflow(local->wake_latency,
+				    parent->wake_latency,
+				    &result->wake_latency))
 		return false;
 	result->enable_parent_state = parent->enable_parent_state;
 	result->level_id = parent->level_id;
